---
title: Example · Checkout board
config:
  look: classic
  theme: dark
  themeVariables:
    cScale0: "#242424"
    cScale1: "#242424"
    cScale2: "#242424"
    cScale3: "#242424"
    cScale4: "#242424"
    cScale5: "#242424"
    cScale6: "#242424"
    cScaleLabel0: "#e0e0e0"
    cScaleLabel1: "#e0e0e0"
    cScaleLabel2: "#e0e0e0"
    cScaleLabel3: "#e0e0e0"
    cScaleLabel4: "#e0e0e0"
    cScaleLabel5: "#e0e0e0"
    cScaleLabel6: "#e0e0e0"
  kanban:
    ticketBaseUrl: "https://tracker.example.com/browse/#TICKET#"
---
%% Top level `id[Column]` is a workflow state; indented `id[Card]` is a work item in it; a bare `Column` / `[Card]` without an id also works.
%% Card metadata `@{ ticket, assigned, priority }`; priority is Very High · High · Low · Very Low; `ticketBaseUrl` links the ticket.
kanban
  backlog[Backlog]
    saved[Saved carts]@{ ticket: SHOP-101, priority: 'Very Low' }
  todo[To do]
    tax[Tax per region]@{ ticket: SHOP-112, assigned: 'backend', priority: 'High' }
  doing[In progress]
    retry[Card retry flow]@{ ticket: SHOP-98, assigned: 'payments', priority: 'Very High' }
  review[In review]
    export[Order export]@{ ticket: SHOP-87, assigned: 'backend', priority: 'Low' }
  done[Done]
    filters[Search filters]@{ ticket: SHOP-75 }
